From dd805eb6a28e9457f38f18216091763961a40349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:18:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] 10.5.8 acceptance: live cutoff, degraded merge, HTTP
 deadline

Live current observation (omitted as_of) uses a judgment cutoff at or
after in-cycle receive times so collected rows are not dropped. Explicit
past as_of still excludes later receives. Provider DEGRADED is not
collapsed to OK. HTTP rejects responses that finish after the monotonic
deadline. News IDs include source; DART pages are de-duplicated; mixed
valid/corrupt market rows are DEGRADED.

Co-authored-by: kssgss94 <kssgss94@gmail.com>
